# A keyword does not match when a name continues it: "if a else b" is the
# keyword form, while "iffy", "if_" and "else1" are plain names. `if` and
# `else` forbid every name byte right after them; the decision between the
# keyword form and a name falls back to the name, and `else` in the middle of
# the keyword form is a syntax error when a name byte follows it directly.
Start
| Statement StatementsTail

StatementsTail@<
| StatementsTail ";" Statement
|

Statement
| Conditional
| Name

Conditional
| "if"@-letter@-digit@-"_" _Blank Name _Blank "else"@-letter@-digit@-"_" _Blank Name

Name
| lowercase_letter _NameTail

_NameTail
| _NameTail letter
| _NameTail digit
| _NameTail "_"
|

_Blank
| _Blank space
|
